From 155616f660a7da858e463bff1e78e9f399fbdaef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Liu <kwliu@nuvoton.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:34:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] spdmd: emit Veraison-verifiable composite EAT from the mock
 attester

The ocp-composite-eat verifier rejected the mock Lead Attester bundle:
the COSE protected header lacked x5t, Lead measurements were encoded as
a text-keyed map instead of [content-format, bstr], the signing key and
UEID were regenerated on every boot (so they could never be enrolled or
chained to an evidence root), and detached Claims-Sets used the legacy
direct-map carriage.

- eat_builder: add x5t [-43, SHA-384(leaf)] to the protected header and
  encode each measurement as [content-format, bstr].
- mock_attester: load a provisioned P-384 key, certificate chain, UEID,
  profile and Concise Evidence measurement from /etc/spdmd/mock-attester
  (fail closed if present but invalid; ephemeral fallback otherwise).
- claims_set_builder/orchestrator: add Record CMW carriage
  {299: [media-type, native evidence, 4]} and select it in spdmd.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [lab mock Lead Attester for QEMU]
Signed-off-by: Joseph Liu <kwliu@nuvoton.com>
